A||||50||TRiAD||OK, (besides Fieros) what's THE most exotic car you've ever driven?||||6||
Z||000000||TRiAD||12-13-2001||12:34 AM||||Well, I'll go first. Here's a pic of the Islero I got to drive this summer. It's a Lamborghini Islero, 4.0 DOHC 48V V12, 6 dual-webbers, FR layout, 2+2 seating, 5sp manual, 4 wheel independant suspension and 4 wheel discs, Campagnalo Magnesium wheels, aluminum body, Leather interior...VERY nice. My favorite Lamborghini, and my favorite "old school" GT car.<P> <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/LouIsleroBridge.jpg"> <P>I have also driven Countach, Diablo, LM002 (LMA, actually), NSX, S2000, Esprits turbo, S2, V8, Viper GTS-R (street), Ferrari 308/328/348, 512 TR, too many Porsches and Vettes to remember, ...and my most unbelieveable ride? RENNtech SL7.4. V12 convertible, faster than ANYTHING I've driven, and more comfortable to boot! My favorite current GT car.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.renntechmercedes.com/splash/cars/slclass/sl7.4.jpg"> <P><I>"The SL 7.4 outfitted by the RENNTech performance team reaches 0-60mph times of 3.9 secs, 0-100mph of 8.6 and a top speed 0f 202mph"</I><P>I have helped out at a few exotic dealers over summers when I was younger and now broker exotics occasionally, when I have someone ask, or something interesting to offer. (It's been REAL slow this year) Otherwise, I'd likely have driven very few, if any, of these cars. <P>Let's see and hear about yours!<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||12-13-2001||12:50 AM||||A Corvair van.  Ohh wait a minute that is about as far from exotic as you can get, but it is rare none the less.  Seriously I think I am going to start hanging out with Triad.  I would love to be able to drive something that was actually designed purely for performance.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||12-13-2001||12:50 AM||||99 Grand Am (with V6)<P>Sad, ain't it?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>Oh, I forgot to add that you suck, Triad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">  <BR><B>86 SE V6 - daily driver</B><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 Sport Coupe 2.5L 5spd (soon to be sold)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
