Z||000021||Mark Matthews||12-13-2001||09:42 AM||||I'd have to say my most exotic would have to be the '57 BelAir in my garage.  Sure they were massed produced, but you don't find them like the one I have in my garage everywhere!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I really need to get some pictures up on the net again.  I've had an offer for $97K for it.  But I don't have it for the money, my great uncle 'gave' it to me.  He knew I liked cars, and knew I would love his!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Survivor:<BR>33,000 original miles on original engine<BR>283 V8 w/ powerglide trans<BR>Original factory paint, still sparkles like an SOB<BR>Original interior, even the clock still works<BR>I take her out about twice a month to keep everything lubed and running good.<P>Anywho, hey Triad, I'd still take the MacLaren F1 over that Lotus anyday!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Did that guy think the dealer was an idiot?  1.5, maybe for the shell?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<p>[This message has been edited by Mark Matthews (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
