Z||000024||yo_sweet||12-13-2001||10:16 AM||||ive driven a 89 iroc z convertable, and a 88 monte carlo ss do these count?<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">   <P> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html</A> <BR>yo_sweet!<p>[This message has been edited by yo_sweet (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||TRiAD||12-13-2001||10:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mark Matthews:<BR><B>...Anywho, hey Triad, I'd still take the MacLaren F1 over that Lotus anyday!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Did that guy think the dealer was an idiot?  1.5, maybe for the shell?!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's not a Lotus, it's a LOTEC C1000. Twin turbo Mercedes V8, fast, fast, fast. 1 of 2 built, the only one with that engine. <BR>He had sent me a check to go look at it for him (as I often do); $1K + expenses for an "in person" evaluation of ANY car. Before I could book the flight, the <I>seller</I> called and killed the deal.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Now, the McLaren F1 GTR is very nice, too, but the guy in Chicago who's selling his (#0069) is STILL trying to get $1.6M for his...I can get the 1995 Lemans winning car for $1.8M, delivered to the US (it's in the UK currently), so the Chicago car is a bit high. <P>If I could get someone to bite on either of them, I'd be set for the next YEAR. (I take 1% from each party on large deals). Man, what I could do with the Fiero with THAT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||MinnGreenGT||12-13-2001||01:29 PM||||A EuroSpec (backwards shifter) 1957 Ferrari 250GT- with a triple-plate racing clutch (the car was setup for vintage racing).<P>Funny story too! I was driving home from my GF's house (this was about 5 or 6 years ago) in my GT (then Gold) and stopped by this guys house. He had an '86 SE sitting out front.  So I struck up a conversation with the guy- turns out he owns 26 cars, of which 2 are old Saab Sonnets, 2 are 57 Ferraris (one restored), 2 or 3 old Lotus Elvan race models and more.  He went in the house, grabbed the keys and fired up the Ferrari!  We stood around talking for awhile and said "you know... I can't start up a car without at least taking it for a spin."  And the rest is history!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
