Z||000046||TRiAD||12-16-2001||02:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PK:<BR><B>Here's probably the worst car ever made in the UK...the Austin Metro.  The standard version had a 1000cc 73bhp engine (when it worked).<P>...<P>Austin then teamed up with the Williams F1 team to produce a rally version.  They ripped out the back seats and stuck in a V6 producing 410hp and made it 4WD.  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/6r4.jpg">  <P>OK so its not exotic and is still pug ugly but it is the fastest thing I've ever sat in!<P>Cheers<BR>PK<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Metro rallye had the Jaguar XJ220 TTV6 in it, and was only rear wheel drive. <P>Nice cars, though!<P>It's still rather have an RS200, or the Peugeot Quasar, if it had seen production...<BR>||||reg||1
